/static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"><img alt=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"The Emperor\"><img alt=\"The Emperor\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Warlock\"><img alt=\"Delusory Warlock\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Pink Tail\"><img alt=\"Pink Tail\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Take out the Strange enemy with no chain, then head to the purple emblem on C4 and use a Multichain to get the last four foes. The bonus line is 16 and the KP Chance is a 90 second win, the purple emblem is Initial BRV Boost so it's easy to meet.\n</p><p>The Strange enemy is the same Fallacious Wanderer as last time with Ragnarok Blade and Dark Flame, but the much better Pupu instead of Behemoth for a summon. Now go Chain them as I said. Delusory Warlock is up first with Float System and Genesis Rock. Next is the False Stalwart with Round Edge, Chain Cast and Cyclone, Weaponsmaster can disperse the winds of Cyclone. Now comes a stronger Stalwart with the same attacks, but naturally a higher level, some equipment, and those EX accessories. He also has an unknown Assist. And then as with the Stalwarts, the fifth and final opponent is a Delusory Warlock, stronger than the first of course, EX accessories, some equipment, Counterfeit Wraith Assist, and the same moveset as the first Warlock.\n</p><p>During this time, thanks to a calendar bonus for AP, Firion mastered Reel Axe and Rope Knife, and thus learned Double Trouble, the HP link for his three core Bravery attacks. After dragging the opponent in, Double Trouble drives them up into the air, then slams them down and away, likely doing wall rush. It's very effective and is definitely worth the AP grinding to get.\n</p><p>The two chests both have Pink Tails.\n</p><p>Approach the end piece, Firion and the Emperor exchange the same banter as the last two times they met, then the Emperor tries to blow Firion up, but his cutscene power seems to have all been spent on that earlier Light Crest because Firion endures.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Emperor_Mateus_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Emperor Mateus (Dissidia PSP)\">The Emperor</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/88/EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110216231129\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"EmperorDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"91\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/88/EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/91?cb=20110216231129\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">3,671\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">22\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">550\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Bombard, Thunder Crest, Landmine, Light Crest, Mine, Dynamite\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Flare, Starfall, Dreary Cell\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Land Worm\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">2/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The Emperor one of the most dangerous end bosses so far. He's got a False Stalwart as Assist, it uses Round Edge and Bardiche when called, and a Land Worm summon to burn through your Bravery like kindling. For accessories, an Earring and Hyper Ring with 7 Near Opponent boosters, and they suit him better than Far from Opponent, actually. His Thunder Crest will be deadly if he catches you in it. He has the usual moveset, but Dreary Cell is a new move I don't believe you've seen from him yet. He creates a spark of light, similar to but distinct from his mines, and he can have up to three out at a time. When you approach that spark, it expends into a rune of energy with orbs of lightning around it, sucking you in as it does so, then explodes to do HP damage. Keep a keen eye on the field so you don't confuse the Cell sparks with his Mines.\n</p><p>And on top of it all, it may just be me but the Emperor seemed to be smarter than previous fights, he kept Thunder Crests and Flares out and was good with his Light Crest to interrupt my attacks, and he was aggressive enough to charge up and use that Assist. Try to keep to the open areas to avoid getting caught in Thunder Crest, as if you do get trapped he'll fire off a Flare to hit you in the face, and after landing an HP hit watch out for his counter Light Crest, as the projectiles are likely to bounce off the walls behind you and hit from your blind spot. Grab EX Cores fast because you don't want the Emperor getting that EX Gauge filled, you never want an opponent in EX Mode of course but his EX Mode bonus is the same HP draining power that Firion has, and with his Flares he's liable to heal himself a significant amount, especially if he uses his Burst. He's a tougher opponent than other end bosses, but is still no match for you. Know that Weaponsmaster can strike through walls, use that to your advantage here.\n</p><p>As the Emperor fades, Firion receives his Crystal, bringing Chapter 6 to a close. You also unlock Report 11, and though it's battle-free it's still funny to watch, it shows how Firion found his wild rose, except then he lost it and Lightning found it...and when Cecil notices Firion watching her, he gets the idea to play matchmaker. Ah, the fun of Ship Tease.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 14\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 11\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 12\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 13\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapt